[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,4.0);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.2,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$20$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {$21$};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$29$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(B)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.8cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
In the right-angled triangle shown, what is the value of $\sec\theta$?
